sp.p:
Verb neuter, not to care; indicative mood, present tense, first person,
                            singular, I do not care; second person, singular, thou dost not care;
                            third person, singular, she does not care.

Show this woman to the end of the avenue. Survey her; mark her well;
                            measure her from top to toe, that you may be sure to know her again; and
                            if ever she dares to darken my doors, put her under the pump.

I've just had a last peep, and now I'm off to my own cottage for another
                            year. Ah, me! I am sadly tired. I cannot walk so well as I used to do;
                            it pains me, standing so many hours, watching outside the Bank.

Now, you hear what I say, sir. I tell you that I am a discharged servant;
                            why, or for what reason, is a mystery to me. Cannot you give me
                            employment?
